I4_1 (space group 80) at P = (1/4, 1/4, 1/4), not a time-reversal-invariant
momentum. A fourfold screw combined with time reversal doubles one of the two
conjugate irreps at P, and the trace of the twofold rotation says which.
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

1. the spinful atomic limit
   realized group   : #80.30 I4_11', s orbitals at Wyckoff 4a and 8b, 12 bands
   P                : (0.25, 0.25, 0.25) in primitive reduced coordinates,
                      and 2P is not a reciprocal-lattice vector
   P valence levels : -2.50036, -2.50036, -2.50036, -2.50036
   χ(E, C2(z))      : (4, 0)
   one fourfold level. The hoppings do not depend on spin, so all of SU(2)
   commutes with H. The level has both irreps and does not say which is doubled

2. the coreps at P, and the rows the irreptables package lists for P
   the coreps at P, χ(E, C2(z)):
      -P3      dim 1   (1, −i)
      -P4P4    dim 2   (2, 2i)
   the rows listed for P, which are the coreps at -P, χ(E, C2(z)):
      -P3P3    dim 2   (2, −2i)
      -P4      dim 1   (1, i)
   each row of one table is the complex conjugate of a row of the other. A label
   depends on whether the table is read at P or at -P. The trace of the twofold
   rotation on a level does not

3. i41_soc('generic', lam=0.4): spin-orbit hoppings averaged over the group
   realized group   : #80.30 I4_11'
   P valence levels : -2.744031, -2.501964, -2.501964, -2.259907
   degeneracies     : 1 + 2 + 1, level gaps 0.242066 and 0.242057

4. the three levels, each labeled from that one diagonalization
   band 0           : E = -2.744031   χ(E, C2(z)) = (1, −i)   -P3
   bands 1 and 2    : E = -2.501964   χ(E, C2(z)) = (2, 2i)   -P4P4
   band 3           : E = -2.259907   χ(E, C2(z)) = (1, −i)   -P3
   doubled corep    : -P4P4, trace 2i on C2(z), two copies of the irrep with trace i
   little group     : unitary part of 2 operations, with one-dimensional irreps
   an antiunitary operation doubles the irrep with χ(C2(z)) = i, so the pair is
   symmetry-enforced. It is not two copies of -P4, an accidental degeneracy, as
   the rows listed for P would make it if they were read as the coreps at P

5. the symmetry data vector of the four valence bands
   valence bands    : -GM5GM7 + -GM6GM8 + -M5M7 + -M6M8 + 2x-N2N2 + 2x-P3 + -P4P4 + 2x-X3X4
   atomic limit     : -1E2E at 4a (21')
   with -P4P4 at P, the symmetry data vector is that of the atomic limit above

6. the control: P6_2 at H
   realized group   : #171.122 P6_21', s orbitals at Wyckoff 3a and 6c, 18 bands
   the coreps at H, χ(E, C3(z), C3^-1(z)):
      -H4      dim 1   (1, −1, 1)
      -H5H6    dim 2   (2, 1, −1)
   lowest 6 bands   : 2x-H4 + 2x-H5H6 at H
   -H5H6 pairs two different irreps. At P, -P4P4 is one irrep doubled

7. the same P-point levels against the spin-orbit strength λ

Done. The figure is written to <FIGDIR>
